.TH DRAWFS 4
.SH NAME
drawfs \- draw device in user space
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B drawfs
[
.B -D
] [
.B -c
.I chan
] [
.B -r
.I width height
] [
.B -s
.I srvname
] [
.B -m
.I mtpt
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Drawfs
is
.IR draw (3)
as a file server: the kernel's devdraw, with
.IR memdraw (2)
and
.IR memlayer (2),
in a process.
It serves the files of
.B #i
.RB ( draw/new ,
.BI draw/ n /colormap\fR,
.BR ctl ,
.BR data ,
.BR refresh ,
and
.BR winname ),
so a program that finds them on
.B /dev
draws through it, unchanged.
Its screen is an image of
.I width
by
.I height
pixels (1024 by 768 by default) in channel
.I chan
.RB ( x8r8g8b8 ),
named
.BI noborder.screen. n
in
.BR winname ;
its memory is a segment of
.IR segment (3),
.BI drawfs. pid\fR.
.PP
For the program that shows the screen,
.B drawfs/screen
reads
.IP
.I segment chan minx miny maxx maxy width
.PP
.RI ( width
in words of 32 bits per line), and
.B drawfs/dirty
the rectangles of the screen drawn on since the last read, a line
.I "minx miny maxx maxy"
each; a read waits for one.
.PP
.I Drawfs
mounts itself before
.I mtpt
.RB ( /dev
by default) and posts
.BI /srv/ srvname
if given.
The
.B -D
flag prints the 9P messages.
.SH EXAMPLE
Draw with a program into a screen of its own, in a new name space:
.IP
.EX
rfork n
drawfs -r 640 480
clock
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/drawfs
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR draw (3),
.IR draw (2),
.IR memdraw (2),
.IR wsys (4)
.SH BUGS
It draws with the processor; the plan (../9front-ui, stage 4c) is to
draw the frequent operations on the GPU.
There is no cursor and no mouse.
